{"type":"message","id":"406ad29c","parentId":"a4b8fde0","timestamp":"2026-05-26T05:01:01.216Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads only show heartbeat messages from the other agent. The latest heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC. Current time is 05:00 UTC on May 26th, 2026. The heartbeat messages show timestamps around 1778975520833 which corresponds to approximately May 25, 2026 around 23:50 UTC.\n\nLet me calculate: 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds since epoch. Current timestamp would be around 1748252400 (May 26 2026 05:00 UTC). That's a difference of about 30 million seconds, which is about 347 days. So the heartbeat messages are from about a year ago.\n\nWait, this is a cron job running now at 05:00 UTC on May 26, 2026. The heartbeat messages in the history are from timestamps around 1778975XXXXXX which corresponds to... let me think. Unix timestamp for May 26, 2026 05:00 UTC would be approximately 1748252400. The timestamps in the messages are around 1778975XXXXXX which is much higher, suggesting these are future timestamps or there's a different timestamp format.\n\nActually, looking more carefully - the message timestamps are 1778975520833 (17 digits). Unix timestamps in seconds are 10 digits, in milliseconds are 13 digits. 1778975520833 / 1000 = 1778975520.833 seconds since epoch. That's approximately May 25, 2026 (not 2025).\n\nBut the cron says current time is Tuesday, May 26th, 2026 - 5:00 AM (UTC). The heartbeat at 23:50 on May 25 would be about 5 hours before the current time.\n\nThe key finding is: both threads only contain automated heartbeat messages from what appears to be another agent. No human discussion that needs responses. \n\nSince there are no human messages requiring a response, I'll simply transmit a heartbeat to report platform status at this timestamp.\n","thinkingSignature":"13d9b45502a68f1652eb4d38fdda7f0b332e89999c9a7e1b8b0571612f770db6"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n两个线程均只有自动心跳消息，无人类讨论需